1
00:00:02,169 --> 00:00:03,409
NARRATOR: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham:

2
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:05,610
FAIRCHILD: Unh. BULLOCK:
The guys call him The Ogre.

3
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,508
He's a serial killer.

4
00:00:08,842 --> 00:00:11,141
Whoever did this,
he's a monster.

5
00:00:11,345 --> 00:00:13,020
The blood of his next
victim is on my hands.

6
00:00:13,044 --> 00:00:14,891
If you don't drop it, that
blood could be Lee's.

7
00:00:14,915 --> 00:00:17,908
The Ogre retaliates against
any cop who investigates him...

8
00:00:18,151 --> 00:00:19,710
kills the people they love.

9
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:21,666
The man who stabbed
Alfred, he's in Gotham.

10
00:00:21,690 --> 00:00:23,066
And you need my
help to find him.

11
00:00:23,090 --> 00:00:24,649
Who sent you?

12
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:27,020
You want me to tell
Bunderslaw you're onto him?

13
00:00:27,828 --> 00:00:29,990
[REGGIE SCREAMS]

14
00:00:44,311 --> 00:00:45,540
MAN: Hey.

15
00:00:48,315 --> 00:00:49,749
You look far from home.

16
00:00:51,451 --> 00:00:53,215
Get away from him.

17
00:00:53,687 --> 00:00:54,848
Or what?

18
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:57,756
[SCOFFS]

19
00:00:58,225 --> 00:01:00,126
Whatever.

20
00:01:05,198 --> 00:01:06,393
SELINA: Come on.

21
00:01:06,833 --> 00:01:10,099
- Did you go back?
- Yeah. The cops are there.

22
00:01:11,371 --> 00:01:12,862
And?

23
00:01:13,941 --> 00:01:16,604
And? What do you think?

24
00:01:16,843 --> 00:01:19,244
He fell out of a five-story
window. He's dead.

25
00:01:21,381 --> 00:01:22,440
Why did you do it?

26
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:25,917
He told us what we wanted, about
Bunderslaw. You didn't have to...

27
00:01:26,119 --> 00:01:28,782
I did. The moment we left,
he was gonna tell his boss!

28
00:01:28,989 --> 00:01:31,117
Who works for you, by the way.

29
00:01:31,525 --> 00:01:35,621
He's the one who tried to kill
me, who tried to kill your butler...

30
00:01:36,229 --> 00:01:38,289
who probably
killed your parents.

31
00:01:38,899 --> 00:01:41,425
I saved your life.

32
00:01:42,302 --> 00:01:46,967
Besides, you wanted to do it
too, you just didn't have the guts.

33
00:01:49,142 --> 00:01:51,077
- Wait...
- Just go home.

34
00:01:51,278 --> 00:01:53,389
We still have to find out who
Bunderslaw is and what we wants.

35
00:01:53,413 --> 00:01:54,642
You mean, you do.

36
00:01:55,048 --> 00:01:56,516
You really think this is over?

37
00:01:56,750 --> 00:01:58,742
He's gonna come after us.

38
00:01:59,987 --> 00:02:02,252
So, what's next? Hm?

39
00:02:06,393 --> 00:02:08,794
- His safe.
- What?

40
00:02:08,996 --> 00:02:11,693
Every senior executive at
Wayne Enterprises has a safe.

41
00:02:12,199 --> 00:02:14,691
Any secrets Bunderslaw
has, that's where they'll be.

42
00:02:14,935 --> 00:02:17,404
- Key or combination?
- Key.

43
00:02:17,604 --> 00:02:18,765
My dad had one.

44
00:02:19,706 --> 00:02:21,902
He'll probably
keep it on him, then.

45
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:26,039
Figure out a way to get
me close, and I'll steal it.

46
00:02:26,279 --> 00:02:28,407
- Can you do that?
- I think so.

47
00:02:28,615 --> 00:02:29,947
And what happened tonight...

48
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:32,779
you tell no one.

49
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:35,055
Not your buddy,
Detective Gordon.

50
00:02:35,288 --> 00:02:37,189
Not your butler.

51
00:02:37,924 --> 00:02:39,153
No one.

52
00:02:58,512 --> 00:03:01,676
Punctures on test subject are
consistent with those on the victim...

53
00:03:01,882 --> 00:03:04,477
indicating the killer
was right-handed.

54
00:03:07,487 --> 00:03:09,388
Yum.

55
00:03:09,823 --> 00:03:10,847
Where's Thompkins?

56
00:03:11,058 --> 00:03:13,618
Detective Gordon, Dr. Thompkins
said I was free to use this room.

57
00:03:13,794 --> 00:03:16,226
She's nice, not like the
old medical examiner...

58
00:03:16,250 --> 00:03:17,822
Ed, just tell me where she is.

59
00:03:18,031 --> 00:03:19,329
No riddles.

60
00:03:19,766 --> 00:03:20,859
Home. She went home.

61
00:03:24,504 --> 00:03:25,665
Hope you find her.

62
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:38,545
[BUZZING]

63
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:43,281
[GLASS SHATTERS
THEN LESLIE GASPS]

64
00:03:45,492 --> 00:03:46,551
Jim?

65
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:51,289
Jim, is that you?

66
00:04:20,026 --> 00:04:22,393
[CAT MEOWS THEN LESLIE GASPS]

67
00:04:27,968 --> 00:04:30,096
You're lucky I don't skin you.

68
00:04:31,972 --> 00:04:33,565
Go on.

69
00:04:36,977 --> 00:04:39,071
[DIALING]

70
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:41,880
[CELL PHONE RINGS]

71
00:04:42,048 --> 00:04:43,368
[LESLIE GASPS THEN
GORDON GRUNTS]

72
00:04:43,817 --> 00:04:45,683
- All right, slow down.
- Lee, please.

73
00:04:45,919 --> 00:04:46,943
Start over.

74
00:04:47,154 --> 00:04:50,591
This case you caught, the dead woman,
she was murdered by a serial killer?

75
00:04:50,791 --> 00:04:53,488
Yes. He's killed a dozen
women, maybe more.

76
00:04:54,127 --> 00:04:57,859
- And Loeb gave you this on purpose?
- He wants to hurt me.

77
00:04:58,431 --> 00:05:00,059
And how am I in danger?

78
00:05:01,101 --> 00:05:05,061
He murders the loved ones of
any cop who investigates him.

79
00:05:05,272 --> 00:05:07,537
That's how he's been able
to get away with it so far.

80
00:05:07,707 --> 00:05:09,300
Anyone who comes after him...

81
00:05:09,509 --> 00:05:13,310
he's killed someone they love,
and the investigation's been buried.

82
00:05:13,513 --> 00:05:16,779
Bullock knows a cop who
came home and found his wife.

83
00:05:18,585 --> 00:05:20,076
Her throat had been cut.

84
00:05:22,823 --> 00:05:24,553
Oh.

85
00:05:24,724 --> 00:05:27,125
That's why Loeb
gave me the case.

86
00:05:27,427 --> 00:05:29,692
Either I give up
like everyone else...

87
00:05:29,896 --> 00:05:32,365
and live knowing I
let a killer go free...

88
00:05:32,899 --> 00:05:34,162
or I keep going...

89
00:05:35,202 --> 00:05:37,171
and someone I love is killed.

90
00:05:41,107 --> 00:05:43,975
- You're not giving up, are you?
- I can't.

91
00:05:45,745 --> 00:05:48,476
That's why I need you to
get out of Gotham right now.

92
00:05:48,915 --> 00:05:50,850
Tonight.

93
00:05:51,151 --> 00:05:52,175
No.

94
00:05:53,553 --> 00:05:56,682
You wanna protect me? Find him.

95
00:05:58,024 --> 00:06:00,118
I'm gonna stay
here and do my job.

96
00:06:04,698 --> 00:06:08,135
But I do like that you
think of me as a loved one.

97
00:06:10,437 --> 00:06:12,133
I do.

98
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:16,373
Love you.

99
00:06:16,810 --> 00:06:20,042
It only took a serial killer
to get you to say that.

100
00:06:25,151 --> 00:06:26,449
[PEOPLE CHATTERING]

101
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:29,055
LENNON: Thanks.
- No problem.

102
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:31,589
[DANCE MUSIC PLAYS
OVER SPEAKERS]

103
00:06:38,665 --> 00:06:40,156
Hi.

104
00:06:52,412 --> 00:06:56,042
[DOOR OPENS THEN CLOSES]

105
00:07:00,453 --> 00:07:02,251
BARBARA: This is it.

106
00:07:02,455 --> 00:07:04,924
Home sweet, you know?

107
00:07:05,792 --> 00:07:08,455
This is a great space.

108
00:07:09,162 --> 00:07:11,131
Selina.

109
00:07:11,898 --> 00:07:15,062
- Hm. Sort of a roommate.
- Hm.

110
00:07:15,235 --> 00:07:17,363
She comes and goes.

111
00:07:20,740 --> 00:07:22,800
- Wayne Enterprises Charity Ball.
- Hm.

112
00:07:23,009 --> 00:07:25,274
Didn't you know I'm
a member of society?

113
00:07:25,645 --> 00:07:30,174
I go every year, get my
picture taken in a pretty dress.

114
00:07:30,850 --> 00:07:32,318
Smile.

115
00:07:46,266 --> 00:07:48,360
Aren't you scared
of my being here?

116
00:07:48,902 --> 00:07:50,871
Should I be?

117
00:07:51,204 --> 00:07:52,832
Are you dangerous?

118
00:07:53,039 --> 00:07:55,338
I don't know. Is your
boyfriend gonna come home?

119
00:07:56,977 --> 00:07:59,378
I never said I had a boyfriend.

120
00:08:07,821 --> 00:08:10,290
I assumed a woman
as beautiful as you...

121
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:11,981
You assumed I had a boyfriend...

122
00:08:12,192 --> 00:08:16,061
and you assumed I would be the
kind of woman who would cheat on him.

123
00:08:16,296 --> 00:08:17,525
Well, I'm not.

124
00:08:17,731 --> 00:08:20,360
And I don't have a boyfriend.

125
00:08:20,867 --> 00:08:23,063
And if a bus hit me tomorrow...

126
00:08:23,303 --> 00:08:25,204
no one would care.

127
00:08:29,342 --> 00:08:32,107
- That change things?
- Yes, actually, it does.

128
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:33,608
Make it more illicit?

129
00:08:33,947 --> 00:08:38,078
Or would there be less chance of us
getting attached one night and done?

130
00:08:38,318 --> 00:08:42,050
Only that would happen anyway,
because once you saw the real me...

131
00:08:42,422 --> 00:08:45,586
you would run screaming,
like everyone else.

132
00:08:47,727 --> 00:08:50,697
I have to say, you're not
who I imagined you would be.

133
00:08:51,064 --> 00:08:52,930
Surprise.

134
00:08:54,401 --> 00:08:55,926
You can let yourself out.

135
00:09:04,677 --> 00:09:06,646
[SINGING] <i>Love, love</i>

136
00:09:07,447 --> 00:09:09,245
<i>Love</i>

137
00:09:09,416 --> 00:09:12,545
But you promised
to dance with me.

138
00:09:12,752 --> 00:09:16,245
And I will. But first, I have
to finish with that gentleman.

139
00:09:17,757 --> 00:09:21,489
Who knew running a
nightclub was so much work?

140
00:09:21,895 --> 00:09:24,626
My poor darling.

141
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,300
<i>But the soul is not deceived</i>

142
00:09:30,470 --> 00:09:31,494
<i>In this world...</i>

143
00:09:31,671 --> 00:09:33,299
As I was saying...

144
00:09:33,506 --> 00:09:36,772
you and your crew are the
best gun and knifemen in the city.

145
00:09:36,976 --> 00:09:39,639
Your hit on Councilman Klein...

146
00:09:39,879 --> 00:09:41,370
a thing of beauty.

147
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:43,777
- I'm a fan.
- Cheers.

148
00:09:44,451 --> 00:09:45,646
What do you want?

149
00:09:45,885 --> 00:09:49,686
For you to help me kill Don
Maroni and all of his lieutenants.

150
00:09:50,156 --> 00:09:52,182
You're having a laugh.

151
00:09:52,525 --> 00:09:54,619
I'm fairly certain I'm not.

152
00:09:54,828 --> 00:09:56,820
And Falcone's good with this?

153
00:09:57,030 --> 00:09:59,397
He will be when it's done.

154
00:09:59,699 --> 00:10:02,430
Thank you. No thank you.

155
00:10:02,635 --> 00:10:04,399
So you like being number two.

156
00:10:06,639 --> 00:10:10,440
Falcone gives Victor Zsasz
first dibs on every new contract.

157
00:10:10,910 --> 00:10:16,008
You bring him the bullet-riddled corpse
of his enemy and all of that will change.

158
00:10:16,416 --> 00:10:18,180
This is your chance to move up.

159
00:10:19,886 --> 00:10:21,616
[CHUCKLING]

160
00:10:21,788 --> 00:10:23,416
You're a mad fellow, aren't you?

161
00:10:25,492 --> 00:10:27,017
Fair enough.

162
00:10:27,227 --> 00:10:29,423
Come by the bar tomorrow...

163
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:30,824
we'll talk details.

164
00:10:37,570 --> 00:10:39,937
- What's this about, Harvey?
BULLOCK: Have a seat.

165
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:42,439
This is my partner, Jim Gordon.

166
00:10:42,642 --> 00:10:44,201
Detective, eight years ago...

167
00:10:44,444 --> 00:10:47,937
you investigated the murder of
a woman named Julie Kemble.

168
00:10:48,148 --> 00:10:50,640
- Yeah, that was a long time
ago. GORDON: It was The Ogre.

169
00:10:50,850 --> 00:10:52,648
Julie Kemble
was his first victim.

170
00:10:52,819 --> 00:10:54,549
But you dropped
the investigation...

171
00:10:54,721 --> 00:10:57,350
and because of that, 11 more
women have been murdered.

172
00:10:57,757 --> 00:11:00,226
- Seriously, guys, you know...
- Stop.

173
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:04,898
We also know The Ogre kills the loved
ones of the cops that hunt him down.

174
00:11:05,999 --> 00:11:07,467
That pattern started with you.

175
00:11:09,068 --> 00:11:11,663
We think you found
something that spooked him.

176
00:11:12,472 --> 00:11:14,998
Your notes from
the investigation.

177
00:11:15,675 --> 00:11:18,110
The last page, something's
been scratched out.

178
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:19,676
I wanna know what.

179
00:11:22,081 --> 00:11:23,674
He killed my wife.

180
00:11:24,250 --> 00:11:26,412
I still got a daughter, Harvey.

181
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:30,114
Beth Tudor.

182
00:11:30,356 --> 00:11:31,915
Katherine Wood.

183
00:11:32,592 --> 00:11:33,616
Jessica Parker.

184
00:11:34,761 --> 00:11:36,093
Eleven women.

185
00:11:38,798 --> 00:11:41,029
Each one was someone's daughter.

186
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:42,892
It has to stop.

187
00:11:44,270 --> 00:11:47,001
Yeah. I was doing
background on the dead girl.

188
00:11:47,207 --> 00:11:51,303
Someone told me she was a nurse
for a private medical clinic uptown.

189
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:55,276
It's on Grant and 80th,
some cosmetic place.

190
00:11:55,515 --> 00:11:58,451
We'll put cops on your
daughter until this is done.

191
00:12:04,991 --> 00:12:06,516
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

192
00:12:20,907 --> 00:12:23,502
- So you forgive
me? KRINGLE: Mm.

193
00:12:25,044 --> 00:12:27,070
- I'll see you tonight.
KRINGLE: Mm-hm.

194
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:34,080
- How's it hanging, Riddle Man?
- Uh, it's hanging...

195
00:12:35,188 --> 00:12:36,918
fine.

196
00:12:39,325 --> 00:12:42,853
Mr. Nygma, did you
need something?

197
00:12:43,329 --> 00:12:44,661
Oh, yes. Uh...

198
00:12:44,864 --> 00:12:49,199
Detective Gordon wanted me to go through
the forensic evidence of these old murders.

199
00:12:49,969 --> 00:12:51,198
Are those bruises?

200
00:12:51,371 --> 00:12:53,135
Uh...

201
00:12:53,306 --> 00:12:54,831
Did Officer Dougherty do that?

202
00:12:55,074 --> 00:12:59,205
Um, he was upset, and he didn't mean
to. I said some things I shouldn't have.

203
00:12:59,445 --> 00:13:01,982
Miss Kringle, this is
not right. He can't just...

204
00:13:02,006 --> 00:13:03,006
Mr. Nygma.

205
00:13:03,583 --> 00:13:05,643
It is none of your concern.

206
00:13:06,853 --> 00:13:10,312
Now, I need to get
started on these files, so...

207
00:13:32,478 --> 00:13:35,107
Alfred. Should you be up?

208
00:13:35,315 --> 00:13:38,717
Thank you, Master Bruce.
I feel... I feel much better.

209
00:13:39,052 --> 00:13:40,384
Can I get you anything?

210
00:13:40,753 --> 00:13:45,487
Yes, actually. I've decided to attend the
Wayne Enterprises Charity Ball tonight.

211
00:13:46,292 --> 00:13:47,636
All the senior
management will be there.

212
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:50,596
People should see that a Wayne
is still the head of the company.

213
00:13:50,763 --> 00:13:52,561
I shall set your
tux out for you.

214
00:13:53,499 --> 00:13:56,333
- Alfred.
- Yes, Master Bruce?

215
00:13:59,872 --> 00:14:02,137
When you were in the army...

216
00:14:02,842 --> 00:14:05,277
you had to kill people, right?

217
00:14:05,845 --> 00:14:08,337
Yes. Yes, I did.

218
00:14:09,449 --> 00:14:11,281
And it was necessary?

219
00:14:11,784 --> 00:14:13,959
I see. So you overheard
the conversation that

220
00:14:13,983 --> 00:14:16,085
Reggie and I had that
was best left unsaid.

221
00:14:16,289 --> 00:14:18,849
But in answer to
your question, yes.

222
00:14:19,058 --> 00:14:21,050
Yes, it was necessary.

223
00:14:22,929 --> 00:14:26,957
Now, if you'll excuse me, I better find
my good cuff links if we're stepping out.

224
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:29,601
No, but you're still recovering.

225
00:14:30,103 --> 00:14:32,902
What, I'm supposed to let you
walk into that nest of vipers?

226
00:14:33,106 --> 00:14:36,873
There'll be hundreds of people
there, Alfred. I won't be in any danger.

227
00:14:37,076 --> 00:14:39,865
So you say, but you're
not gonna go alone.

228
00:14:39,889 --> 00:14:41,104
I won't be alone.

229
00:14:42,815 --> 00:14:44,977
I've invited Selina Kyle.

230
00:14:45,218 --> 00:14:47,187
Selina Kyle?

231
00:14:47,387 --> 00:14:50,084
To the Wayne Enterprises Ball?

232
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:52,554
I see.

233
00:14:53,292 --> 00:14:54,590
What do you see?

234
00:14:54,794 --> 00:14:57,628
Nothing. I mean, you know,
you're a healthy young lad...

235
00:14:57,830 --> 00:15:01,460
and she's a pretty girl with a
penchant of wearing too much leather...

236
00:15:01,701 --> 00:15:04,432
- Alfred, it's not like that.
- Then what's it like?

237
00:15:06,439 --> 00:15:09,603
Well, what if it is, huh?

238
00:15:09,809 --> 00:15:11,141
What's wrong with that?

239
00:15:12,445 --> 00:15:14,437
Absolutely nothing.

240
00:15:15,248 --> 00:15:19,618
So I will wait in the car outside
so you don't feel my watchful eye.

241
00:15:19,819 --> 00:15:22,755
But I will be close
by if the need's be.

242
00:15:23,823 --> 00:15:25,815
That is the deal.

243
00:15:26,359 --> 00:15:27,657
Fine.

244
00:15:28,094 --> 00:15:31,792
Could you call around and send some
dresses and shoes to where she's staying?

245
00:15:33,132 --> 00:15:35,158
This is the address.

246
00:15:36,502 --> 00:15:38,095
It's a charity ball, Alfred.

247
00:15:39,639 --> 00:15:41,267
I'll be fine.

248
00:15:49,982 --> 00:15:51,848
BULLOCK: Freaky, huh?

249
00:15:52,251 --> 00:15:54,652
I wonder how they
recognize themselves after.

250
00:15:56,189 --> 00:15:57,953
Doc Thompkins is fine.

251
00:15:58,124 --> 00:16:00,320
No one's gonna touch
her at the precinct. Relax.

252
00:16:00,526 --> 00:16:03,257
You do understand it's because
of me that she's in danger?

253
00:16:03,463 --> 00:16:05,125
Anything that
happens is my fault.

254
00:16:05,331 --> 00:16:08,699
You can't hold yourself responsible
for the actions of a psychopath.

255
00:16:08,901 --> 00:16:10,665
Sure I can.

256
00:16:10,870 --> 00:16:14,136
Detectives. I'm Dr. Cushman.
How can I help you?

257
00:16:14,340 --> 00:16:17,674
We're looking into the murder
of a woman named Julie Kemble.

258
00:16:17,877 --> 00:16:21,814
- She worked here about eight years
ago. CUSHMAN: Of course. Terrible thing.

259
00:16:22,014 --> 00:16:23,812
Julie was a talented nurse.

260
00:16:24,016 --> 00:16:26,485
But she'd only just started
here when it happened.

261
00:16:26,686 --> 00:16:28,848
She'd been recommended
by one of our patients.

262
00:16:29,322 --> 00:16:32,349
- Patient's name?
- I'm afraid I can't give you that.

263
00:16:32,558 --> 00:16:33,856
Confidentiality.

264
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:35,221
BULLOCK: Really?

265
00:16:35,561 --> 00:16:37,530
You're gonna make
us get a warrant?

266
00:16:38,097 --> 00:16:39,326
Yes.

267
00:16:39,532 --> 00:16:42,593
"I specialize in fake boobs, but
I got ethics, I need a warrant."

268
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:45,669
We'll talk to Judge
Harkness. I'm sure...

269
00:16:48,741 --> 00:16:51,210
That car was in
front of the precinct.

270
00:16:51,944 --> 00:16:53,003
BULLOCK: Jim, wait up.

271
00:16:59,986 --> 00:17:01,045
[ENGINE STARTS]

272
00:17:01,721 --> 00:17:02,745
[TIRES SCREECHING]

273
00:17:12,331 --> 00:17:14,232
- You sure about this?
- It was him.

274
00:17:14,433 --> 00:17:16,334
- You saw his face?
- No.

275
00:17:16,502 --> 00:17:19,631
I should've been looking for a tail.
It's obvious he tracks our investigations.

276
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:22,865
Called in a description of
the car and a partial plate.

277
00:17:23,276 --> 00:17:24,642
So, what's the next move?

278
00:17:24,877 --> 00:17:27,608
Gordon. You got a
call, says it's urgent.

279
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:34,892
GORDON: Gordon. LENNON
[OVER PHONE]: <i>Detective.</i>

280
00:17:34,921 --> 00:17:37,288
I didn't get to say hello
properly in the alley.

281
00:17:37,490 --> 00:17:39,550
- Listen to me.
<i>- Don't bother tracing this.</i>

282
00:17:40,126 --> 00:17:42,357
I'm giving you one
chance to turn yourself in.

283
00:17:42,562 --> 00:17:45,657
You make me come after
you and I will put you down.

284
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:48,766
Something tells me you've
begun to buy your own press.

285
00:17:49,869 --> 00:17:55,001
The hero cop who's gonna clean up
Gotham. The rising star of the G.C.P.D.

286
00:17:55,241 --> 00:17:58,234
- I'll stop you, that's for damn sure.
- No, detective, you won't.

287
00:17:58,444 --> 00:18:00,811
Keep on, and I will
kill someone you love.

288
00:18:01,013 --> 00:18:03,278
This is your only warning.

289
00:18:03,449 --> 00:18:05,315
[LINE CLICKS THEN DIAL TONE]

290
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:11,080
Oh, no. Tell me that wasn't him.

291
00:18:14,627 --> 00:18:18,587
He's used to intimidating cops. We
have to show him we're not afraid.

292
00:18:18,965 --> 00:18:20,797
And how do we do that?

293
00:18:24,203 --> 00:18:26,968
- You're okay with this, you're sure?
- Yes.

294
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:28,908
It's the right thing to do.

295
00:18:35,247 --> 00:18:38,115
[CAMERA SHUTTERS CLICKING]

296
00:18:38,284 --> 00:18:40,719
I called you here today...

297
00:18:40,953 --> 00:18:43,097
because the people of
Gotham deserve to know

298
00:18:43,121 --> 00:18:45,288
that there's a serial
killer in their midst.

299
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:48,792
For years, he's
killed with impunity...

300
00:18:48,995 --> 00:18:52,363
aided by a culture of silence
and fear among the police.

301
00:18:53,466 --> 00:18:55,128
That ends now.

302
00:18:55,501 --> 00:18:58,994
We'll be providing the names
and photos of all of the victims.

303
00:18:59,205 --> 00:19:01,003
Please call with
any information.

304
00:19:01,207 --> 00:19:03,676
And to the man who
committed these horrific crimes...

305
00:19:04,143 --> 00:19:06,703
<i>your days of hiding are over.</i>

306
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:09,640
<i>I'm coming after you...</i>

307
00:19:10,683 --> 00:19:12,811
<i>and I'm not gonna stop.</i>

308
00:19:21,961 --> 00:19:23,190
What are those for?

309
00:19:23,396 --> 00:19:25,160
The Wayne Charity Ball.

310
00:19:25,531 --> 00:19:29,263
It's boring but good for
the gallery's business.

311
00:19:29,502 --> 00:19:30,812
Well, I'll probably
see you there.

312
00:19:30,836 --> 00:19:31,997
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

313
00:19:32,171 --> 00:19:33,469
What?

314
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:35,198
I'm going with Bruce Wayne.

315
00:19:35,741 --> 00:19:37,039
Wait, what?

316
00:19:38,110 --> 00:19:39,976
MAN 1: Delivery for
Selina Kyle. SELINA: Oh.

317
00:19:40,146 --> 00:19:42,615
Uh, over there.

318
00:19:46,752 --> 00:19:48,983
MAN 2: Thank you. Enjoy.

319
00:19:54,226 --> 00:19:56,627
Am I really supposed
to wear these?

320
00:19:57,196 --> 00:20:00,633
Okay. We have
a lot of work to do.

321
00:20:06,739 --> 00:20:09,903
Got it. That was the doctor.
Harkness sent over the warrant.

322
00:20:10,109 --> 00:20:13,910
The dead girl came to the clinic by
way of a Miss Constance Van Groot.

323
00:20:14,413 --> 00:20:17,042
Van Groot? That's one of
Gotham's oldest families. Shipping.

324
00:20:17,249 --> 00:20:20,413
We thought The Ogre might be
rich. Could be the old lady had a son.

325
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:22,955
GORDON: You got an address?
- Right here.

326
00:20:23,122 --> 00:20:27,583
WOMAN [SINGING]:
<i>You're the cream in my coffee</i>

327
00:20:28,828 --> 00:20:31,627
Well, Butch, Connor
and his crew are onboard.

328
00:20:31,831 --> 00:20:34,096
- They hate Maroni even more than I...
- Shut up.

329
00:20:34,734 --> 00:20:36,225
Maroni and his crew are here.

330
00:20:37,002 --> 00:20:39,267
- I couldn't turn them away.
- Of course. No matter...

331
00:20:39,472 --> 00:20:41,236
No. She was already here.

332
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:43,170
MARONI: Is that my buddy Oswald?

333
00:20:43,943 --> 00:20:45,809
- Come here.
- Oh, Oswald.

334
00:20:46,245 --> 00:20:49,738
WOMAN [SINGING]: <i>You
will always be my necessity</i>

335
00:20:49,915 --> 00:20:51,440
<i>I'd be lost without you</i>

336
00:20:51,617 --> 00:20:53,176
[MARONI CHUCKLES]

337
00:20:53,753 --> 00:20:55,153
There he is.

338
00:20:55,988 --> 00:20:57,650
Mother, what are you doing?

339
00:20:58,157 --> 00:21:01,457
- I am having a drink with Mister...
- Ah, ah, ah.

340
00:21:01,660 --> 00:21:03,652
I told you. Sal.

341
00:21:04,864 --> 00:21:05,923
With Sal.

342
00:21:07,066 --> 00:21:09,433
- But we shouldn't impose any longer...
- Ah, ah, ah.

343
00:21:10,569 --> 00:21:16,008
- You're not taking my Gertrud.
- Oh, his Gertrud. Heh-heh-heh.

344
00:21:16,175 --> 00:21:17,973
Sit. Join us.

345
00:21:18,177 --> 00:21:20,339
GERTRUD: Oswald, sit.

346
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:22,772
Sit, Oswald.

347
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:24,541
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

348
00:21:28,487 --> 00:21:29,887
Hello.

349
00:21:30,122 --> 00:21:31,215
I'm Bruce Wayne.

350
00:21:31,457 --> 00:21:33,153
- Barbara Kean. BRUCE: Oh.

351
00:21:33,325 --> 00:21:35,521
Selina never said you're
who she's staying with.

352
00:21:35,728 --> 00:21:37,219
Detective Gordon spoke of you.

353
00:21:38,397 --> 00:21:40,628
Well, Selina can
be a little guarded.

354
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:44,529
- Yes, I know. SELINA:
Stop talking about me.

355
00:21:50,309 --> 00:21:52,141
Selina...

356
00:21:54,046 --> 00:21:55,412
You look very nice.

357
00:21:56,048 --> 00:21:58,244
The shoes hurt.

358
00:21:58,851 --> 00:22:01,821
Have fun. Look
for me at the ball.

359
00:22:02,021 --> 00:22:03,990
It was nice meeting you.

360
00:22:07,860 --> 00:22:09,556
Think she's here?

361
00:22:13,265 --> 00:22:15,564
Miss Van Groot?

362
00:22:16,235 --> 00:22:18,568
G.C.P.D.

363
00:22:18,771 --> 00:22:21,138
I need to say this
is not exactly legal.

364
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:23,502
We're running out of time.

365
00:22:23,676 --> 00:22:25,269
[CLATTERING]

366
00:22:26,812 --> 00:22:28,610
[GASPING]

367
00:22:28,948 --> 00:22:30,678
Over here.

368
00:22:42,962 --> 00:22:44,362
He's good.

369
00:22:44,563 --> 00:22:47,226
Call it in. I'm gonna go
check the rest of the house.

370
00:22:57,376 --> 00:22:58,810
He told me...

371
00:22:59,044 --> 00:23:01,275
but I was too slow.

372
00:23:04,783 --> 00:23:06,081
Hello?

373
00:23:11,724 --> 00:23:13,784
Miss Van Groot?

374
00:23:15,561 --> 00:23:18,053
I'm a police officer.

375
00:23:19,999 --> 00:23:21,991
Miss Van Groot?

376
00:23:38,817 --> 00:23:39,841
Oh.

377
00:23:40,219 --> 00:23:41,847
Gordon!

378
00:23:43,088 --> 00:23:45,023
Jim!

379
00:23:48,661 --> 00:23:50,527
Jim Gordon...

380
00:23:50,829 --> 00:23:53,094
Constance Van Groot.

381
00:24:02,808 --> 00:24:06,245
[CLASSICAL MUSIC
PLAYS OVER SPEAKERS]

382
00:24:06,412 --> 00:24:08,608
[PEOPLE CHATTERING]

383
00:24:19,959 --> 00:24:22,292
Everyone's staring at us.

384
00:24:22,861 --> 00:24:24,762
Well, I am Bruce Wayne.

385
00:24:26,632 --> 00:24:28,225
Well, I am.

386
00:24:28,634 --> 00:24:30,364
I don't see Bunderslaw anywhere.

387
00:24:31,637 --> 00:24:33,162
He's probably not coming.

388
00:24:33,372 --> 00:24:35,637
But he's on the guest list.

389
00:24:36,008 --> 00:24:37,271
Just keep dancing.

390
00:24:38,377 --> 00:24:40,278
And smile, maybe.

391
00:24:42,948 --> 00:24:44,678
Name's Jacob Skolimski.

392
00:24:44,883 --> 00:24:48,115
He's not talking, but near as we
can tell he was the old lady's butler.

393
00:24:48,320 --> 00:24:50,812
You think The Ogre's this
guy's son, not the dead woman's?

394
00:24:51,023 --> 00:24:53,549
<i>Yeah. Coroner said the old
bird's been dead for years.</i>

395
00:24:53,726 --> 00:24:56,286
My guess, Ogre killed her,
daddy pretends she's alive...

396
00:24:56,462 --> 00:24:59,660
so his crazy serial killer son
can keep living off her money.

397
00:24:59,865 --> 00:25:01,026
He tried to kill himself.

398
00:25:01,266 --> 00:25:04,031
He knew you were closing in. He
has to be in contact with his son.

399
00:25:04,269 --> 00:25:07,068
Yeah. Listen, Gordon's running
pretty hot on this one, cap.

400
00:25:07,306 --> 00:25:09,832
Can you blame him? Thinks
Thompkins is the next victim.

401
00:25:10,042 --> 00:25:12,409
<i>Still, watch him.</i>

402
00:25:12,644 --> 00:25:13,873
Alvarez called.

403
00:25:14,546 --> 00:25:16,412
Nothing on the
son in the system.

404
00:25:16,648 --> 00:25:18,776
We have to make him talk.

405
00:25:19,818 --> 00:25:22,982
GORDON: Make this simple. Give
us your son's name and address.

406
00:25:23,188 --> 00:25:24,520
JACOB: Or what?

407
00:25:25,057 --> 00:25:26,821
I'm not afraid of you.

408
00:25:28,994 --> 00:25:30,826
Only because you don't know me.

409
00:25:31,730 --> 00:25:33,892
Listen, I get wanting
to protect your son.

410
00:25:34,099 --> 00:25:36,027
But how many more
women will he have to kill

411
00:25:36,051 --> 00:25:38,002
before you realize he
needs to be locked up?

412
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:39,933
What are you talking about?

413
00:25:40,172 --> 00:25:44,576
Don't play dumb with me. You were hiding
a rotting corpse upstairs for years...

414
00:25:44,810 --> 00:25:46,335
but no, no, my son's an angel.

415
00:25:46,545 --> 00:25:49,344
He didn't murder close to a
dozen women that we know of.

416
00:25:49,548 --> 00:25:53,610
My son, he made
one mistake. One.

417
00:25:53,852 --> 00:25:56,083
Anything else is lies.

418
00:25:58,223 --> 00:26:00,089
So tell us the truth.

419
00:26:01,693 --> 00:26:04,561
[PEOPLE CHATTERING]

420
00:26:06,965 --> 00:26:08,900
Selina, what
happened last night...

421
00:26:09,568 --> 00:26:11,867
- can't happen again.
- I didn't have a choice.

422
00:26:12,071 --> 00:26:13,403
I don't accept that.

423
00:26:13,806 --> 00:26:15,206
[SELINA SCOFFS]

424
00:26:15,374 --> 00:26:17,707
I knew you wouldn't
be able to handle it.

425
00:26:18,410 --> 00:26:19,878
You're right.

426
00:26:20,079 --> 00:26:23,049
- I did wanna kill him.
- Keep your voice down.

427
00:26:24,283 --> 00:26:27,048
But there's a line, Selina.
You can say I don't have guts...

428
00:26:27,252 --> 00:26:29,300
but the fact is I
will never cross it.

429
00:26:29,324 --> 00:26:31,656
I guess that's where
we're different, then.

430
00:26:32,558 --> 00:26:34,584
Because if I had to
do it again, I would.

431
00:26:36,161 --> 00:26:39,598
And it wouldn't
bother me one bit.

432
00:26:45,404 --> 00:26:46,428
[INAUDIBLE DIALOGUE]

433
00:26:46,605 --> 00:26:47,732
That's Bunderslaw.

434
00:26:53,979 --> 00:26:56,847
[CHATTERING]

435
00:26:57,850 --> 00:26:59,011
[CLEARS THROAT]

436
00:27:00,619 --> 00:27:03,680
- Riddle Man.
- Officer Dougherty, a word.

437
00:27:11,964 --> 00:27:14,490
I can start a war or end one.

438
00:27:14,700 --> 00:27:17,534
I can give you the strength of
heroes or leave you powerless.

439
00:27:18,103 --> 00:27:21,471
I might be snared with a glance,
but no force can compel me to stay.

440
00:27:23,308 --> 00:27:24,901
What am I?

441
00:27:25,644 --> 00:27:28,443
- You got me.
- Love.

442
00:27:28,947 --> 00:27:33,112
Miss Kringle has given hers to
you, and in return you hurt her.

443
00:27:33,919 --> 00:27:36,946
- I saw the bruises.
- And?

444
00:27:37,523 --> 00:27:39,549
And you cannot do that.

445
00:27:39,791 --> 00:27:42,103
- The next time you do that, I'll...
DOUGHERTY: Whoa, whoa, whoa.

446
00:27:42,127 --> 00:27:44,460
Calm down. You'll
give yourself a girly fit.

447
00:27:45,130 --> 00:27:46,928
Have you ever been with a woman?

448
00:27:49,168 --> 00:27:50,932
Didn't think so.

449
00:27:52,437 --> 00:27:54,838
They need a firm hand.

450
00:27:55,574 --> 00:27:59,170
That goes double for
Kringle. The girl's got a tongue.

451
00:28:00,145 --> 00:28:01,204
I won't let you hurt her.

452
00:28:01,380 --> 00:28:02,473
[LAUGHS]

453
00:28:02,648 --> 00:28:04,480
Oh, yeah?

454
00:28:08,787 --> 00:28:10,483
What are you gonna do?

455
00:28:13,825 --> 00:28:15,384
[CLICKS TONGUE]

456
00:28:15,594 --> 00:28:17,460
That's what I thought.

457
00:28:20,032 --> 00:28:22,524
Later, Riddle Man.

458
00:28:27,673 --> 00:28:29,733
[CLASSICAL MUSIC
PLAYS OVER SPEAKERS]

459
00:28:32,377 --> 00:28:34,403
Care to dance?

460
00:28:37,282 --> 00:28:39,581
- You.
- Me.

461
00:28:40,652 --> 00:28:43,178
JACOB: It was not a
place for a boy to grow up.

462
00:28:43,689 --> 00:28:46,625
Miss Van Groot kept herself
sealed off from the world...

463
00:28:46,858 --> 00:28:49,851
but she doted on my son.

464
00:28:50,128 --> 00:28:51,494
Treated him as her own.

465
00:28:51,797 --> 00:28:55,063
Still, I... I didn't realize
how deep it went.

466
00:28:55,267 --> 00:28:58,294
This kid's mom was out of the
picture, so he started thinking...

467
00:28:58,470 --> 00:29:00,530
he was this Van Groot
woman's secret son.

468
00:29:00,739 --> 00:29:05,609
I tried to tell him it wasn't true,
but he had built this fantasy...

469
00:29:05,811 --> 00:29:07,370
and Miss Van Groot led him on.

470
00:29:07,579 --> 00:29:10,845
She was deranged. Cruel, even.

471
00:29:11,016 --> 00:29:12,644
So about 10 years
ago, he confronts her.

472
00:29:12,884 --> 00:29:17,219
He demands that she acknowledge him, give
him her last name, put him in the will.

473
00:29:17,422 --> 00:29:18,788
She laughs at him.

474
00:29:19,024 --> 00:29:22,085
Said it was all just a
big joke. So he kills her.

475
00:29:22,494 --> 00:29:24,622
His dad feels guilty,
helps him cover it up.

476
00:29:24,830 --> 00:29:27,322
So the old woman rejects
him, he kills her, bang.

477
00:29:27,499 --> 00:29:30,264
You got a serial killer with a
mommy-didn't-love-me complex.

478
00:29:30,469 --> 00:29:31,960
But there's a wrinkle.

479
00:29:32,170 --> 00:29:34,537
I don't know where my son is.

480
00:29:34,940 --> 00:29:37,341
He called today, told me
the police would be coming.

481
00:29:37,576 --> 00:29:41,570
But I haven't seen him since
the day he killed Miss Van Groot.

482
00:29:42,848 --> 00:29:46,285
My son is not a bad man.

483
00:29:48,186 --> 00:29:52,146
Your son has been seducing and
killing women for almost a decade.

484
00:29:52,391 --> 00:29:56,385
[LAUGHING]

485
00:29:57,262 --> 00:29:58,855
Why is he laughing?

486
00:29:59,097 --> 00:30:02,124
My son? Seducing women?

487
00:30:03,602 --> 00:30:07,664
Let me show you my son. Two
pictures. That's all I managed to save.

488
00:30:08,206 --> 00:30:10,766
You've heard "a face
only a mother could love"?

489
00:30:11,677 --> 00:30:14,579
Well, his mother couldn't.

490
00:30:14,780 --> 00:30:16,715
She left us after he was born.

491
00:30:16,948 --> 00:30:19,110
Oh, yes. My son...

492
00:30:19,318 --> 00:30:21,219
the seducer.

493
00:30:27,726 --> 00:30:30,457
It makes sense he scratched
his face out of those pictures.

494
00:30:30,662 --> 00:30:32,631
But that means this
can't be The Ogre.

495
00:30:32,831 --> 00:30:34,390
We're chasing the wrong guy.

496
00:30:34,633 --> 00:30:35,828
Jim had an idea.

497
00:30:36,034 --> 00:30:38,196
Judge Harkness'
warrant was very specific.

498
00:30:38,403 --> 00:30:40,599
- I don't have to say anything.
- Then nod.

499
00:30:40,806 --> 00:30:43,105
Did you operate on this man?

500
00:30:44,109 --> 00:30:48,376
I need to know what he looks like now,
or the next woman he kills will be on you.

501
00:30:54,920 --> 00:30:57,981
[CLASSICAL MUSIC
PLAYS OVER SPEAKERS]

502
00:31:05,597 --> 00:31:10,092
Never, never would he
play with other children.

503
00:31:10,469 --> 00:31:14,600
He knew even then he
was too good for them.

504
00:31:14,806 --> 00:31:19,244
And now he is a
respectable man of business...

505
00:31:19,444 --> 00:31:21,709
my Oswald.

506
00:31:21,913 --> 00:31:24,576
Well, this has been a delight.

507
00:31:25,083 --> 00:31:26,312
But it's late.

508
00:31:26,551 --> 00:31:28,281
One thing...

509
00:31:28,487 --> 00:31:29,921
Gertrud, my love.

510
00:31:30,088 --> 00:31:32,956
- Oh.
- A question that's been bothering me.

511
00:31:33,191 --> 00:31:35,786
Oh, no. Oh, no.

512
00:31:35,994 --> 00:31:37,428
Is this an act?

513
00:31:39,264 --> 00:31:40,789
[GERTRUD AND MARONI CHUCKLE]

514
00:31:40,966 --> 00:31:44,630
Are you pretending that
he's just a nightclub owner?

515
00:31:45,103 --> 00:31:48,232
- Or are you really that stupid?
- Stop!

516
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:50,341
I don't understand. I...

517
00:31:50,575 --> 00:31:52,840
- Your son...
- Don Maroni, I am warning you!

518
00:31:53,078 --> 00:31:55,274
- Is a coldblooded psychopath.
- No, no, no.

519
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:57,972
I can't count how
many men he's killed.

520
00:31:58,216 --> 00:32:02,085
My own friend, Frankie Carbone,
he stabbed him a dozen times.

521
00:32:02,287 --> 00:32:06,748
What kind of person plunges a
knife into someone over and over?

522
00:32:06,958 --> 00:32:08,722
He's a filthy liar, Mother!

523
00:32:08,927 --> 00:32:11,453
He's just angry because
I played him for a fool.

524
00:32:11,663 --> 00:32:12,687
[GERTRUD GASPS]

525
00:32:12,998 --> 00:32:15,160
You know, don't you?

526
00:32:15,367 --> 00:32:17,529
- I can see it.
- Let go of her!

527
00:32:17,769 --> 00:32:20,500
Did you catch him one night
washing blood from his hands?

528
00:32:20,739 --> 00:32:24,403
When did you realize that you
had given birth to a monster?

529
00:32:24,576 --> 00:32:26,204
GERTRUD: Aah! Aah!

530
00:32:31,850 --> 00:32:34,012
You're going to pay for this.

531
00:32:34,753 --> 00:32:36,016
Maybe.

532
00:32:36,254 --> 00:32:40,157
Or maybe this ends with me
dumping your lifeless body into the river.

533
00:32:40,358 --> 00:32:44,125
Either way, you and Mama
Gertrud can stop pretending.

534
00:32:48,166 --> 00:32:49,759
The place is looking good.

535
00:32:53,004 --> 00:32:54,768
Shh, shh, shh.

536
00:32:57,576 --> 00:33:00,080
The other night, when
you saw my invitation,

537
00:33:00,104 --> 00:33:02,344
why didn't you tell
me you were coming?

538
00:33:02,547 --> 00:33:05,381
I wasn't. I didn't get invited.

539
00:33:05,584 --> 00:33:08,053
Oh, so you're crashing.

540
00:33:08,286 --> 00:33:11,085
Oh, no, I'm on the list.

541
00:33:11,256 --> 00:33:13,851
It's amazing what a
$10,000 donation will do.

542
00:33:14,493 --> 00:33:18,396
You donated
$10,000 to this? Why?

543
00:33:18,597 --> 00:33:20,930
I was hoping that
would be apparent.

544
00:33:24,936 --> 00:33:27,064
And what if I
decided not to come?

545
00:33:27,305 --> 00:33:31,106
Well, then, I'd have been making
a generous donation to charity...

546
00:33:32,110 --> 00:33:35,740
and I would have
been very disappointed.

547
00:33:55,333 --> 00:33:58,098
[DOOR OPENS THEN CLOSES]

548
00:34:02,274 --> 00:34:06,575
The way things ended
last night, it was my fault.

549
00:34:07,045 --> 00:34:08,877
But I felt something.

550
00:34:09,080 --> 00:34:10,639
I couldn't let it slip away.

551
00:34:10,982 --> 00:34:12,883
Well, that's very sweet, but...

552
00:34:13,084 --> 00:34:17,579
You said that when people see
the real you, they run screaming.

553
00:34:19,858 --> 00:34:24,455
Someone said the same thing to me
once, that no one would ever love me.

554
00:34:25,864 --> 00:34:28,629
- Who?
- The woman I thought was my mother.

555
00:34:29,935 --> 00:34:33,099
Barbara, I know
what it's like...

556
00:34:33,305 --> 00:34:37,470
to be one person on the inside
and have the world see another.

557
00:34:38,243 --> 00:34:40,109
I lived like that...

558
00:34:40,378 --> 00:34:44,179
and it almost destroyed me.
I can see it destroying you.

559
00:34:46,318 --> 00:34:47,786
I don't wanna dance anymore.

560
00:34:47,986 --> 00:34:50,182
The person that I am now...

561
00:34:50,422 --> 00:34:51,515
I created.

562
00:34:52,123 --> 00:34:55,025
I brought him into being.

563
00:34:55,961 --> 00:34:58,260
I can do the same for you.

564
00:34:59,764 --> 00:35:02,029
Aren't you tired
of playing games?

565
00:35:04,102 --> 00:35:05,627
Of hiding?

566
00:35:10,542 --> 00:35:12,101
Yes.

567
00:35:18,683 --> 00:35:20,675
MAN 1: Goodbye.
MAN 2: See you soon.

568
00:35:21,953 --> 00:35:24,980
- Hello. I'm Bruce Wayne.
- Sid Bunderslaw.

569
00:35:26,124 --> 00:35:29,686
BRUCE: I'm going around trying to get to
know everybody who works for the company.

570
00:35:30,295 --> 00:35:32,735
- You work for Wayne Enterprises,
don't you? BUNDERSLAW: I do.

571
00:35:32,931 --> 00:35:35,025
I'm the Director of
Physical Operations...

572
00:35:35,467 --> 00:35:37,436
which I'm afraid is a bit dull.

573
00:35:37,636 --> 00:35:39,935
There are many much
more interesting people here.

574
00:35:40,639 --> 00:35:43,131
Well, I'm sure I'll get to
meet everyone eventually.

575
00:35:43,942 --> 00:35:46,434
Forgive me, Bruce, I have
an early flight tomorrow.

576
00:35:46,645 --> 00:35:48,238
It's been a pleasure.

577
00:35:48,847 --> 00:35:50,338
It was, um...

578
00:35:51,149 --> 00:35:52,481
It was nice meeting you.

579
00:35:57,088 --> 00:35:58,716
SELINA: Sorry.

580
00:36:00,325 --> 00:36:01,816
[BRUCE SIGHS]

581
00:36:04,262 --> 00:36:07,858
See? Nothing to it.

582
00:36:13,738 --> 00:36:15,229
What is it?

583
00:36:19,377 --> 00:36:21,073
Nothing.

584
00:36:31,389 --> 00:36:32,982
Stop right there, buster.

585
00:36:35,860 --> 00:36:39,797
Riddle Man? What the hell are
you doing creeping around here?

586
00:36:40,365 --> 00:36:43,267
- You need to leave Miss Kringle alone.
- What?

587
00:36:44,502 --> 00:36:47,802
I'm not gonna let you
hurt her, ever again.

588
00:36:49,040 --> 00:36:52,533
I think you need to
leave Gotham tonight.

589
00:36:52,711 --> 00:36:55,044
[LAUGHING]

590
00:36:55,914 --> 00:36:58,008
I get it now.

591
00:36:58,216 --> 00:36:59,775
You got a thing for my girl.

592
00:37:01,586 --> 00:37:03,521
That's too funny.

593
00:37:06,591 --> 00:37:08,025
Don't take this personal.

594
00:37:08,426 --> 00:37:10,486
[NYGMA GRUNTS THEN COUGHS]

595
00:37:10,662 --> 00:37:11,721
Aw.

596
00:37:11,896 --> 00:37:12,955
[DOUGHERTY LAUGHS]

597
00:37:13,665 --> 00:37:15,896
You want some more?

598
00:37:16,101 --> 00:37:17,933
Upsy-daisy! Unh!

599
00:37:20,739 --> 00:37:21,763
Oh, dear.

600
00:37:29,347 --> 00:37:31,976
[GRUNTING]

601
00:37:40,458 --> 00:37:41,949
Riddle Man...

602
00:37:43,762 --> 00:37:44,786
Oh, dear.

603
00:37:45,830 --> 00:37:47,423
Oh, dear.

604
00:37:47,632 --> 00:37:49,157
Oh, no.

605
00:37:50,268 --> 00:37:51,566
[LAUGHS]

606
00:37:56,207 --> 00:37:57,835
Oh, dear.

607
00:37:58,009 --> 00:38:00,376
[LAUGHING]

608
00:38:02,881 --> 00:38:04,008
Oh, dear.

609
00:38:06,184 --> 00:38:07,948
Oh, dear.

610
00:38:17,695 --> 00:38:20,392
- Oswald.
- Feeling better?

611
00:38:20,632 --> 00:38:22,533
I made tea.

612
00:38:23,034 --> 00:38:27,597
I'm afraid you had, well,
heh, a little too much to drink.

613
00:38:28,640 --> 00:38:31,838
Mr. Maroni, he... He has
a strange sense of humor...

614
00:38:32,043 --> 00:38:33,409
Oswald.

615
00:38:33,645 --> 00:38:38,310
I am not some bumpkin from
the country with hay in my brains.

616
00:38:38,983 --> 00:38:41,475
- No.
- I am your mother...

617
00:38:41,686 --> 00:38:45,214
and I will love you
no matter what.

618
00:38:46,157 --> 00:38:48,649
But lie to me now...

619
00:38:49,828 --> 00:38:52,491
and you will break my heart.

620
00:38:54,566 --> 00:38:56,865
Oswald...

621
00:38:58,503 --> 00:39:01,439
have you done things...

622
00:39:01,673 --> 00:39:03,164
you should not?

623
00:39:08,079 --> 00:39:10,048
Mother...

624
00:39:10,248 --> 00:39:13,343
I'm a nightclub owner. Hm?

625
00:39:13,518 --> 00:39:14,781
That's all.

626
00:39:25,530 --> 00:39:27,055
I'm tired now.

627
00:39:29,033 --> 00:39:31,298
I am tired.

628
00:39:39,277 --> 00:39:43,715
[SOBBING]

629
00:39:43,882 --> 00:39:45,783
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

630
00:39:54,792 --> 00:39:57,057
Yeah, I got a delivery
for Gertrud from Sal.

631
00:39:57,262 --> 00:39:59,390
Tip's not included.

632
00:39:59,898 --> 00:40:01,992
You tell Sal it's over.

633
00:40:02,233 --> 00:40:06,000
The guns are bought.
The killing room is waiting.

634
00:40:06,237 --> 00:40:09,139
He doesn't know it,
but he's a dead man.

635
00:40:17,649 --> 00:40:20,414
On second thought,
I'll tell him myself.

636
00:40:21,920 --> 00:40:23,650
[GRUNTING]

637
00:40:29,027 --> 00:40:30,962
GERTRUD: Oswald?

638
00:40:31,162 --> 00:40:32,721
Who was that?

639
00:40:33,498 --> 00:40:35,865
It's Mr. Yatsko from next door.

640
00:40:36,100 --> 00:40:38,365
He needs help
taking out some trash.

641
00:40:38,536 --> 00:40:41,005
GERTRUD: You... You...
Please, you help him, then.

642
00:40:49,614 --> 00:40:50,980
Jason Van Groot?

643
00:40:51,182 --> 00:40:54,812
His real name is Jason Skolimski. He
used the old woman's name at the clinic.

644
00:40:55,019 --> 00:40:58,649
But there's no Jason Van Groot or
Skolimski in Gotham. The guy's a ghost.

645
00:40:58,990 --> 00:41:01,357
So the old woman rejects
him, he goes to the doctor...

646
00:41:01,559 --> 00:41:03,221
gets himself a pretty new face.

647
00:41:03,394 --> 00:41:05,124
That's where he
runs into the nurse.

648
00:41:05,330 --> 00:41:06,798
And we're off to the races.

649
00:41:06,998 --> 00:41:10,696
- I don't suppose you got a picture?
- Missing from the file. No surprise there.

650
00:41:10,902 --> 00:41:13,838
But the good doctor was
kind enough to do a sketch.

651
00:41:14,038 --> 00:41:16,803
It's been 10 years since he
last saw him, but it's a start.

652
00:41:17,008 --> 00:41:19,671
So we have his real name,
but not what alias he's using...

653
00:41:19,877 --> 00:41:23,006
or what he looks like
beyond a decade-old sketch.

654
00:41:23,214 --> 00:41:25,376
Did he say anything
else on the phone today?

655
00:41:25,583 --> 00:41:29,577
- Anything we might have missed?
GORDON: No, just wanted me to back off.

656
00:41:29,921 --> 00:41:34,689
Told me not to believe my own
press as the rising star of the G.C.P.D.

657
00:41:37,595 --> 00:41:39,496
What is it?

658
00:41:39,864 --> 00:41:42,060
The paper that said that...

659
00:41:42,300 --> 00:41:45,236
they ran an old photo
of me from a charity gala.

660
00:41:46,204 --> 00:41:47,228
I wasn't alone.

661
00:41:55,580 --> 00:41:57,913
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

662
00:41:58,116 --> 00:41:59,846
GORDON: Barbara?

663
00:42:00,351 --> 00:42:01,410
Is Barbara here?

664
00:42:01,619 --> 00:42:04,088
- No. Why?
- Where is she?

665
00:42:04,389 --> 00:42:05,988
When's the last
time you saw her?

666
00:42:06,012 --> 00:42:08,053
At the Wayne Ball.
She left with some guy.

667
00:42:08,960 --> 00:42:11,759
- Was this the guy?
- That's kind of a crappy drawing.

668
00:42:12,130 --> 00:42:13,325
Was this the guy?

669
00:42:16,134 --> 00:42:18,228
Yeah, I think so.

670
00:42:18,770 --> 00:42:20,739
Why? Who is he?

671
00:42:31,616 --> 00:42:32,743
What's through there?

672
00:42:33,918 --> 00:42:35,079
See for yourself.

673
00:43:49,894 --> 00:43:51,886
[English - US -SDH]
